# 必考词 Unit28
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit28核心高频词汇

{{envision}}{/ɪnˈvɪʒn/}}{v. 想象；展望}}{{It is hard to envision a world without the internet.}}

{{episode}}{/ˈepɪsəʊd/}}{n. 一段经历；插曲}}{{The most dramatic episode in the story occurs in chapter five.}}

{{epoch}}{/ˈiːpɒk/}}{n. 时代；纪元}}{{The invention of the printing press marked a new epoch in history.}}

{{equivalent}}{/ɪˈkwɪvələnt/}}{adj. 等价的；n. 等价物}}{{The two qualifications are not equivalent in the job market.}}

{{erode}}{/ɪˈrəʊd/}}{v. 侵蚀；腐蚀}}{{Public trust in the institution has been eroded over time.}}

{{erroneous}}{/ɪˈrəʊniəs/}}{adj. 错误的；不正确的}}{{The erroneous report caused confusion among investors.}}

{{espionage}}{/ˈespiənɑːʒ/}}{n. 间谍活动；谍报}}{{The country was accused of industrial espionage.}}

{{esteem}}{/ɪˈstiːm/}}{n. 尊重；v. 尊敬}}{{She is held in high esteem by her colleagues.}}

{{ethnic}}{/ˈeθnɪk/}}{adj. 民族的；种族的}}{{The city has a rich ethnic diversity.}}

{{evacuate}}{/ɪˈvækjueɪt/}}{v. 疏散；撤离}}{{Residents were evacuated before the hurricane hit.}}

{{evoke}}{/ɪˈvəʊk/}}{v. 唤起；引起}}{{The music evoked memories of her childhood.}}

{{exempt}}{/ɪɡˈzempt/}}{adj. 被免除的；v. 免除}}{{Small businesses are exempt from certain taxes.}}

{{exert}}{/ɪɡˈzɜːrt/}}{v. 施加；运用}}{{The teacher exerted a positive influence on her students.}}

{{explicit}}{/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/}}{adj. 明确的；直言的}}{{The contract contains explicit terms and conditions.}}

{{exploit}}{/ɪkˈsplɔɪt/}}{v. 开发；剥削；n. 功绩}}{{The company was accused of exploiting natural resources unsustainably.}}

{{exponential}}{/ˌekspəˈnenʃl/}}{adj. 指数的；急剧增长的}}{{The exponential growth of data presents new challenges.}}

{{extract}}{/ɪkˈstrækt/}}{v. 提取；摘录}}{{The machine extracts juice from fresh fruits.}}

{{fabricate}}{/ˈfæbrɪkeɪt/}}{v. 捏造；制造}}{{The evidence was fabricated to frame the innocent man.}}

{{facilitate}}{/fəˈsɪlɪteɪt/}}{v. 促进；使便利}}{{The new road facilitates access to the rural community.}}

{{faction}}{/ˈfækʃn/}}{n. 派系；小集团}}{{The political party was divided into rival factions.}}

{{famine}}{/ˈfæmɪn/}}{n. 饥荒}}{{The drought led to a severe famine in the region.}}

{{fascinate}}{/ˈfæsɪneɪt/}}{v. 使着迷；吸引}}{{The documentary fascinated viewers with its stunning visuals.}}

{{fate}}{/feɪt/}}{n. 命运；天数}}{{She believed that fate had brought them together.}}

{{fatigue}}{/fəˈtiːɡ/}}{n. 疲劳；v. 使疲劳}}{{Mental fatigue can affect your ability to concentrate.}}

{{feasible}}{/ˈfiːzəbl/}}{adj. 可行的；可能的}}{{The engineers determined that the project was technically feasible.}}

{{federation}}{/ˌfedəˈreɪʃn/}}{n. 联邦；联合会}}{{The country is a federation of several autonomous states.}}

{{forge}}{/fɔːrdʒ/}}{v. 锻造；伪造}}{{The two nations forged a strong alliance after the war.}}

{{formidable}}{/ˈfɔːrmɪdəbl/}}{adj. 强大的；令人敬畏的}}{{The team faced a formidable opponent in the final.}}

{{foster}}{/ˈfɒstər/}}{v. 培养；促进}}{{The program fosters creativity and critical thinking in students.}}

{{fraction}}{/ˈfrækʃn/}}{n. 分数；小部分}}{{Only a fraction of the population has access to clean water.}}

{{fragile}}{/ˈfrædʒaɪl/}}{adj. 脆弱的；易碎的}}{{The peace agreement remains fragile and could collapse at any time.}}

{{friction}}{/ˈfrɪkʃn/}}{n. 摩擦；不和}}{{There is friction between the two departments over budget分配.}}

{{furnish}}{/ˈfɜːrnɪʃ/}}{v. 提供；装备；布置}}{{The apartment is fully furnished with modern appliances.}}

{{futile}}{/ˈfjuːtaɪl/}}{adj. 无用的；徒劳的}}{{All attempts to negotiate were futile.}}

{{galaxy}}{/ˈɡæləksi/}}{n. 银河系；星系}}{{The Milky Way is just one of billions of galaxies in the universe.}}

{{gear}}{/ɡɪər/}}{n. 齿轮；装备；v. 调整}}{{The company is gearing up for the holiday season.}}

{{gene}}{/dʒiːn/}}{n. 基因}}{{Genes play a significant role in determining physical traits.}}

{{genocide}}{/ˈdʒenəsaɪd/}}{n. 种族灭绝}}{{The international community condemned the genocide in the region.}}

{{genuine}}{/ˈdʒenjuɪn/}}{adj. 真正的；真诚的}}{{The painting was confirmed to be a genuine masterpiece.}}

{{glamour}}{/ˈɡlæmər/}}{n. 魅力； glamour}}{{The glamour of Hollywood attracts aspiring actors from around the world.}}
